{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00267",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 4.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.36,
      "end_seconds": 9.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.7,
      "end_seconds": 14.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.66,
      "end_seconds": 18.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "I've been losing weight without trying."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.72,
      "end_seconds": 24.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.8,
      "end_seconds": 26.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "About... well, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.75,
      "end_seconds": 30.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.26,
      "end_seconds": 35.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get loss of appetite as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.75,
      "end_seconds": 42.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.51,
      "end_seconds": 47.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Okay, so tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.36,
      "end_seconds": 50.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.23,
      "end_seconds": 54.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.98,
      "end_seconds": 59.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "The loss of appetite? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.26,
      "end_seconds": 65.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.79,
      "end_seconds": 69.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.89,
      "end_seconds": 74.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "So, have you had any blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.85,
      "end_seconds": 79.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Not at all, no blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.95,
      "end_seconds": 83.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "So, have you had any diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.34,
      "end_seconds": 85.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "No, no diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 88.91,
      "end_seconds": 93.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice diarrhoea. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 100.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Uh, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.15,
      "end_seconds": 110.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Let me check a few things. Any coughing up blood, chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.03,
      "end_seconds": 122.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "No, no coughing up blood, no chest pain, no shortness of breath. I did have night sweats at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.32,
      "end_seconds": 125.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Alright, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.13,
      "end_seconds": 128.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Nothing there, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.11,
      "end_seconds": 132.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "So, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.14,
      "end_seconds": 135.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.43,
      "end_seconds": 139.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.87,
      "end_seconds": 144.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 145.96,
      "end_seconds": 153.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the Glycomet was 250 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.94,
      "end_seconds": 157.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.08,
      "end_seconds": 170.03,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. So, I take iron tablets, once a day for my blood count. I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.0,
      "end_seconds": 174.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.51,
      "end_seconds": 182.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "No, it's at home. I'd been on rosuvastatin, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.64,
      "end_seconds": 185.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.1,
      "end_seconds": 190.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "No, um, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.51,
      "end_seconds": 194.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.1,
      "end_seconds": 212.0,
      "duration_seconds": 16.9,
      "text": "Not really, uh, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.41,
      "end_seconds": 215.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.27,
      "end_seconds": 220.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack. My father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.34,
      "end_seconds": 235.05,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.45,
      "end_seconds": 238.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.27,
      "end_seconds": 242.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.65,
      "end_seconds": 266.38,
      "duration_seconds": 22.73,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I've had low haemoglobin for nearly five years now. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I've never really been one for hospitals. Um, I have high cholesterol, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.54,
      "end_seconds": 275.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Alright. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. Okay, low haemoglobin, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.42,
      "end_seconds": 280.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.91,
      "end_seconds": 281.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.47,
      "end_seconds": 292.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 294.3,
      "end_seconds": 301.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 109 over 78, pulse is 101 beats a minute, saturation 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.82,
      "end_seconds": 302.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.62,
      "end_seconds": 306.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.08,
      "end_seconds": 310.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.34,
      "end_seconds": 327.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Air entry is a bit reduced at the top of the right lung."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.82,
      "end_seconds": 331.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Okay, breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.05,
      "end_seconds": 350.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I can feel a couple of small glands in your neck, not tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.12,
      "end_seconds": 378.92,
      "duration_seconds": 23.8,
      "text": "So, that's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with an infection or something chronic going on, I can't say what yet at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out a thyroid problem yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.91,
      "end_seconds": 383.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "It could also be tuberculosis, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.96,
      "end_seconds": 390.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Well, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.44,
      "end_seconds": 407.52,
      "duration_seconds": 16.08,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an infection or something chronic going on, I can't say what yet, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been losing weight without trying for six months, and no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.41,
      "end_seconds": 411.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Oh, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.99,
      "end_seconds": 420.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "We should do a sputum test for chronic cough. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.11,
      "end_seconds": 423.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Okay, you know, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.58,
      "end_seconds": 453.56,
      "duration_seconds": 28.98,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for weight loss. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. We should do a chest X-ray for weight loss and cough. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Weigh yourself once a week at the same time and note it down. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'll also refer you to the chest clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.96,
      "end_seconds": 460.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.47,
      "end_seconds": 462.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.21,
      "end_seconds": 471.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "If you cough up blood or get breathless, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.69,
      "end_seconds": 474.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Okay, um, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 475.81,
      "end_seconds": 478.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 479.8,
      "end_seconds": 483.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.57,
      "end_seconds": 490.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 491.11,
      "end_seconds": 495.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "So, um, I come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 497.05,
      "end_seconds": 502.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 503.08,
      "end_seconds": 506.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, uh, doctor, thanks."
    }
  ]
}